  "interpretation": "Descriptive counts of how the R13 double behaves under frozen oracles. B interrupted on L1-C02-a is the double's designed stop-on-drift switch; the evaluation convention scores an interrupted attempt as not-completed, so that cell reads as a B shortfall although it is the designed behaviour. A completes the drift case only because the double ignores drift. The oracles are derived from the same owned scenarios as the double, so they are not independent of it.",
  "label": "synthetic-control",
  "limits": "Plumbing only. Descriptive-only under D3 (one holdout lineage, 1 and 4 units against a minimum of 19; reasons below-D3-minimum and repeated-within-lineage); no noninferiority verdict, no utility, refinement, library, inferential, economic, adoption or promotion claim. Arm C equals arm A by construction (keep-base) and arm D was not run. The synthetic-control rows are verdict-ineligible and excluded from every D4 verdict. Not computed: false safe admissions, missed safe parallelism, correction and review effort, interrupted-recovery, conflict precision and recall (the double has no such notions). Costs: every measure is unknown (no exporter, no reservations); cost claims are blocked, and the authorized EUR 0 is a statement that no paid route exists, not an observed invoice. The one discovery base probe is outside the T012 ledger. No host, model, native session, paid route or human annotation. Reviews by Claude subagents are not independent Luna review.",
  "method": "python3.13 -m tests.harness_t005_cohort: build six Units, run a keep-base round whose only probe is the R13 double on discovery L2-C01-a, register the five L1 holdout cases with arms A, B and C (C is A), run the double once per unit and arm, observe, commit, grade with each unit's FixtureOracle and report with harness_evaluation.evaluate.",
